  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>knot</keyword>
  <short_description>Create a trefoil knot surface.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>[X, Y, Z] = knot()</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[X, Y, Z] = knot(n)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>knot()</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>knot(n)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>knot(ax, n)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>n</param_name>
      <param_description
      >Number of facets around the tube cross-section: positive whole number (default 16).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>ax</param_name>
      <param_description>Target axes: &apos;axes&apos; object.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>X, Y, Z</param_name>
      <param_description
      >x-, y-, and z- coordinates of the knot surface without drawing it.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>
      <b>knot</b> builds and plots a smooth tube swept around a trefoil
      knot curve (the classic (2,3) torus knot).</p>
    <p>The curve is analytic, so the tube is generated by sweeping a
      circular cross-section along the Frenet frame (tangent, principal
      normal and binormal) of the curve.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
